WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.333
Mark, Chapter Five.

2
00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:06.400
And they came over unto the other side of the sea, into the country of the Gadarenes.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:22.133
And when he was come out of the ship, immediately there met him out of the tombs a man with an unclean spirit, Who had his dwelling among the tombs; and no man could bind him, no, not with chains: Because that he had been often bound with fetters and chains,

4
00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:29.333
and the chains had been plucked asunder by him, and the fetters broken in pieces: neither could any man tame him.

5
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:36.133
And always, night and day, he was in the mountains, and in the tombs, crying, and cutting himself with stones.

6
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:45.333
But when he saw Jesus afar off, he ran and worshipped him, And cried with a loud voice, and said, What have I to do with thee, Jesus, thou Son of the most high God?

7
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:48.533
I adjure thee by God, that thou torment me not.

8
00:00:48.533 --> 00:00:52.400
For he said unto him, Come out of the man, thou unclean spirit.

9
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.467
And he asked him, What is thy name?

10
00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:59.733
And he answered, saying, My name is Legion: for we are many.

11
00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:03.867
And he besought him much that he would not send them away out of the country.

12
00:01:03.867 --> 00:01:08.267
Now there was there nigh unto the mountains a great herd of swine feeding.

13
00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:14.667
And all the devils besought him, saying, Send us into the swine, that we may enter into them.

14
00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:17.333
And forthwith Jesus gave them leave.

15
00:01:17.333 --> 00:01:27.200
And the unclean spirits went out, and entered into the swine: and the herd ran violently down a steep place into the sea, (they were about two thousand;) and were choked in the sea.

16
00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.933
And they that fed the swine fled, and told it in the city, and in the country.

17
00:01:30.933 --> 00:01:33.200
And they went out to see what it was that was done.

18
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:42.000
And they come to Jesus, and see him that was possessed with the devil, and had the legion, sitting, and clothed, and in his right mind: and they were afraid.

19
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.933
And they that saw it told them how it befell to him that was possessed with the devil, and also concerning the swine.

20
00:01:48.933 --> 00:01:52.267
And they began to pray him to depart out of their coasts.

21
00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:58.267
And when he was come into the ship, he that had been possessed with the devil prayed him that he might be with him.

22
00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:08.800
Howbeit Jesus suffered him not, but saith unto him, Go home to thy friends, and tell them how great things the Lord hath done for thee, and hath had compassion on thee.

23
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:17.067
And he departed, and began to publish in Decapolis how great things Jesus had done for him: and all men did marvel.

24
00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:26.000
And when Jesus was passed over again by ship unto the other side, much people gathered unto him: and he was nigh unto the sea.

25
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:42.133
And, behold, there cometh one of the rulers of the synagogue, Jairus by name; and when he saw him, he fell at his feet, And besought him greatly, saying, My little daughter lieth at the point of death: I pray thee, come and lay thy hands on her, that she may be healed; and she shall live.

26
00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:46.667
And Jesus went with him; and much people followed him, and thronged him.

27
00:02:46.667 --> 00:03:03.733
And a certain woman, which had an issue of blood twelve years, And had suffered many things of many physicians, and had spent all that she had, and was nothing bettered, but rather grew worse, When she had heard of Jesus, came in the press behind, and touched his garment.

28
00:03:03.733 --> 00:03:08.000
For she said, If I may touch but his clothes, I shall be whole.

29
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:14.000
And straightway the fountain of her blood was dried up; and she felt in her body that she was healed of that plague.

30
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:22.133
And Jesus, immediately knowing in himself that virtue had gone out of him, turned him about in the press, and said, Who touched my clothes?

31
00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:28.400
And his disciples said unto him, Thou seest the multitude thronging thee, and sayest thou, Who touched me?

32
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:32.400
And he looked round about to see her that had done this thing.

33
00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:39.200
But the woman fearing and trembling, knowing what was done in her, came and fell down before him, and told him all the truth.

34
00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:45.333
And he said unto her, Daughter, thy faith hath made thee whole; go in peace, and be whole of thy plague.

35
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:54.267
While he yet spake, there came from the ruler of the synagogue's house certain which said, Thy daughter is dead: why troublest thou the Master any further?

36
00:03:54.267 --> 00:04:01.467
As soon as Jesus heard the word that was spoken, he saith unto the ruler of the synagogue, Be not afraid, only believe.

37
00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:07.467
And he suffered no man to follow him, save Peter, and James, and John the brother of James.

38
00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:14.533
And he cometh to the house of the ruler of the synagogue, and seeth the tumult, and them that wept and wailed greatly.

39
00:04:14.533 --> 00:04:19.467
And when he was come in, he saith unto them, Why make ye this ado, and weep?

40
00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:22.267
the damsel is not dead, but sleepeth.

41
00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:24.267
And they laughed him to scorn.

42
00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:33.333
But when he had put them all out, he taketh the father and the mother of the damsel, and them that were with him, and entereth in where the damsel was lying.

43
00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:41.867
And he took the damsel by the hand, and said unto her, Talitha cumi; which is, being interpreted, Damsel, I say unto thee, arise.

44
00:04:41.867 --> 00:04:47.067
And straightway the damsel arose, and walked; for she was of the age of twelve years.

45
00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:49.600
And they were astonished with a great astonishment.

46
00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:55.467
And he charged them straitly that no man should know it; and commanded that something should be given her to eat.

